 "titulo": "The last stand of the 300 ⚔️ Thermopylae Part 3 #story #shorts",
 "capa": "GO TELL THE SPARTANS",
 "descripcion": "Betrayed by a mountain path, Leonidas sends the allies home and stays with his 300, plus Thespians and Thebans, for the last stand on a small hill.\n\nWould you have stayed?\n\nFrom Herodotus, Histories, book 7 (chapters 175-228). Herodotus gives millions of Persians; modern historians estimate roughly 100,000 to 300,000.\n#thermopylae #sparta #300 #ancienthistory #shorts",
 "visual": "3d",
 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "At dawn, the lookouts ran down the mountain *screaming*.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "The Persians are behind us. Ephialtes showed them the path.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "The pass was lost. Everyone knew it.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Leonidas sent most of the Greek allies home, to fight another day.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Three hundred Spartans stayed. And seven hundred men from Thespiae refused to leave.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Stay, because what they did with their last morning still has no equal.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "They didn't wait behind the wall anymore. They *charged*.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Out into the open, straight into the Persian army.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Their spears broke. They fought on with swords.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Leonidas fell. The Spartans fought four times to recover his body, and won it back.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then they pulled back to a small hill, back to back.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Herodotus says they fought with swords, then hands, then *teeth*.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Until arrows covered the hill, and the last one fell.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Xerxes won the pass. But Greece had time to prepare.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "That same year, the Persian fleet was crushed at Salamis.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Later, the poet Simonides wrote a line for their stone.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Go tell the Spartans, stranger passing by, that here, obedient to their laws, we lie.",
   "pausa": 0.8
  },
  {
   "texto": "All because you woke up as one of three hundred.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
